{"output":"I’ll inspect the search logic and existing tests, make a focused fix, then run the tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nEvery completed request currently updates state, even if a newer search has started. I added a request ID check for results, errors, and loading. Clearing the query also invalidates pending requests. I’ll run the existing tests and a focused race-condition probe.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search updates results, loading, or errors. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe; git diff --check. Exit code 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search updates results, loading, or errors. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe; git diff --check. Exit code 0.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":11,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-batching-iincv9nu/search-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":186,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-f5d0e5ea9bcb3610c264e940f47c31f7.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nnode --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst item = title => [{ id: title, title, url: '/' }];\nfor (const staleFails of [false, true]) {\n  for (const finishLatestFirst of [false, true]) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const latest = c.search('latest');\n    if (finishLatestFirst) { requests[1].resolve(item('latest')); await latest; }\n    const before = c.getState();\n    if (staleFails) requests[0].reject(new Error('stale')); else requests[0].resolve(item('old'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (!finishLatestFirst) { requests[1].resolve(item('latest')); await latest; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'latest', results: item('latest'), loading: false, error: null });\n    const pending = c.search('pending');\n    const cleared = c.search('  ');\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n    if (staleFails) requests[2].reject(new Error('stale')); else requests[2].resolve(item('pending'));\n    await Promise.all([pending, cleared]);\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Race-condition probe passed');\nJS\n git diff --check && git diff -- src/search/controller.ts && git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-batching-iincv9nu/search-2-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":368,"stdout_bytes":2174,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-49be87bb1f25b77f597477e892bc7d53.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":43140,"output_tokens":1071},"usage